*20
/        QUESTIONS:
/1.  LAKE ELSINORE IS CONSIDERED BY LEGEND TO BE
/(A) BEAUTIFUL (B) TEMPORARY (C) FULL OF GOLD (D) CURSED
	D
/2.   THIS LAKE IS LOCATED (A) IN A VOLCANIC CRATER
/(B) IN THE DESERT (C) IN A VALLEY (D) NEAR THE OCEAN
	C
/3.   DURING THE NINETIES THE LAKE WAS FAMOUS (A) AS A
/RESORT (B) AS THE CENTER OF A MINING AREA (C) AS A 
/STOPPING PLACE FOR PEOPLE GOING WEST (D) AS A PONY
/EXPRESS STATION
	A
/4.   CHIEF TONDO WAS (A) A KIND MAN (B) A STERN MAN
/(C) A GREAT LEADER WHO UNITED TWO TRIBES (D) A BITTER
/ENEMY OF THE WHITE MAN
	B
/5.   PROBABLY CHIEF TONDO"S RAGE WAS DUE TO THE FACT
/THAT (A) PALO WAS NOT WEALTHY ENOUGH (B) MORNING STAR
/WAS TOO YOUNG TO MARRY (C) TONDO"S TRIBE AND PALO"S
/TRIBE WERE ENEMIES (D) PALO HAD MURDERED TONDO"S BROTHER
	C
/6.   MORNING STAR AND PALO FINALLY (A) MARRIED (B) KILLED
/TONDO (C) KILLED THEMSLEVES (D) WALKED TO THEIR DEATH IN
/THE LAKE
	D
/7.   OLD-TIMERS TELL OF A GREAT UPHEAVAL IN THE LAKE.
/THEY SAY THAT AT THAT TIME, THE WATER TURNED (A) RED
/(B) BLUE (C) GREEN (D) YELLOW
	A
/8.   WHEN BOATS WERE MYSTERIOUSLY OVERTURNED IN THE LAKE,
/THEIR OCCUPANTS (A) SWAM ASHORE (B) RIGHTED THE BOATS
/(C) HAD TO AVOID VICIOUS FISH (D) USUALLY NEVER RETURNED
	D
/9.   ON TWO OCCASIONS, FISH IN THE LAKE (A) SUDDENLY DIED
/(B) BECAME PLENTIFUL (C) DEVELOPED WEIRD SHAPES
/(D) BECAME VERY LARGE
	A
/10.   WHEN THE LAKE DRIED UP IN 1951, IT WAS FOUND THAT
/(A) THERE WAS AN OLD VOLCANIC CRATER AT THE BOTTOM
/(B) THERE WERE DEEP TRENCHES AT THE BOTTOM (C) THERE
/WERE RELICS OF INDIANS ON THE BOTTOM (D) THERE WERE NO
/TRACES OF DISTURBANCES ON THE BOTTOM
	D
